WEBVTT

01:02.390 --> 01:05.844
[Episode 12: Because of Love]

01:47.602 --> 01:51.740
[36 Hours Before the Sell-off]

01:58.881 --> 02:00.127
Would you care for a drink?

02:00.127 --> 02:02.461
I believe we are done talking.

02:03.175 --> 02:04.727
Hold on...

02:06.204 --> 02:09.175
We regret what we didn't do more,

02:09.175 --> 02:13.555
and unfulfilled love lingers far longer.

02:13.555 --> 02:15.107
Do you recall saying that?

02:17.048 --> 02:19.482
"Face every challenge. Never back down.

02:19.482 --> 02:21.678
I won't let you leave Haemu with regrets

02:21.678 --> 02:23.663
over the things you failed to try."

02:24.748 --> 02:27.309
I was quite moved by that specific part

02:27.309 --> 02:30.046
of your inaugural speech.

02:33.175 --> 02:35.358
You should keep your word.

02:35.358 --> 02:37.562
Don't let me live with any regrets.

02:46.578 --> 02:49.049
You brought decent liquor. What a shame.

02:50.437 --> 02:52.344
I quit drinking entirely.

02:54.009 --> 02:56.028
Then I'll just have it all myself.

03:05.718 --> 03:07.707
You have a surprisingly sharp memory.

03:08.474 --> 03:11.342
Even I forgot about making that promise.

03:11.342 --> 03:14.338
I honestly thought we got a great leader

03:15.050 --> 03:16.461
back in those days.

03:19.277 --> 03:21.029
That actually stings a bit.

03:23.617 --> 03:25.325
I'm being completely serious.

03:25.325 --> 03:26.938
Around that particular time,

03:27.551 --> 03:30.224
the company seemed like a total joke.

03:30.224 --> 03:34.563
Bosses were clueless, peers were slow.

03:34.563 --> 03:36.694
This place just felt way too small for me.

03:42.175 --> 03:43.593
Yes,

03:43.593 --> 03:46.589
I was incredibly arrogant back then.

03:46.589 --> 03:48.925
My life felt like, I don't know,

03:48.925 --> 03:53.186
speeding down a wide open highway.

03:53.186 --> 03:55.384
Until I finally crossed paths with her.

03:55.384 --> 03:57.551
In Ah slammed the brakes

03:57.551 --> 04:00.151
on your perfectly smooth life.

04:00.151 --> 04:01.903
Demoted you to PM, right?

04:01.903 --> 04:03.941
It was a harsh reality check.

04:03.941 --> 04:06.390
Why am I even doing this garbage?

04:07.174 --> 04:09.244
After thinking like that for a while,

04:09.244 --> 04:11.479
I suddenly felt deeply ashamed of myself.

04:12.534 --> 04:14.415
To me, the workplace was simply

04:14.415 --> 04:16.702
a tool to achieve things, get recognized,

04:16.702 --> 04:19.403
and constantly prove my own worth.

04:21.009 --> 04:23.075
But to someone else out there,

04:23.075 --> 04:25.655
this company is their life's pride.

04:25.655 --> 04:26.656
I should get going now.

04:26.656 --> 04:28.871
It's their joyful daily routine,

04:38.481 --> 04:41.943
and something they must fiercely protect.

04:41.943 --> 04:42.800
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

04:42.800 --> 04:43.718
I realized that a company is

04:43.718 --> 04:44.737
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

04:44.737 --> 04:47.765
ultimately a place
where real people spend their lives.

04:50.592 --> 04:53.913
I hope you take a close look at them.

04:53.913 --> 04:55.477
You don't want

04:57.551 --> 04:59.594
any regrets either, right?

05:28.615 --> 05:29.634
[Jeon Jae Yeol]

05:32.259 --> 05:33.769
Hello?

05:36.634 --> 05:37.829
What?

05:40.043 --> 05:42.180
Excuse me.

05:52.126 --> 05:53.139
Want some coffee?

05:53.139 --> 05:54.548
No, I'm perfectly fine.

05:54.548 --> 05:56.333
I'll get him out of here fast.

05:57.634 --> 06:00.188
Ki Jun, wake up.

06:00.188 --> 06:01.856
Oh, hey.

06:01.856 --> 06:02.882
When did you get here?

06:02.882 --> 06:05.485
Exactly how much did you drink?

06:05.485 --> 06:07.247
And why are you totally wasted alone?

06:07.247 --> 06:08.738
I know, right?

06:08.738 --> 06:11.974
I only had a few, but I totally passed out.

06:14.551 --> 06:16.145
What is this thing?

06:18.206 --> 06:20.407
Did you cover me up with this?

06:20.407 --> 06:22.818
Oh, I'm actually a little touched.

06:23.782 --> 06:26.297
Cut the nonsense already.

06:26.297 --> 06:28.174
Let's get straight to the point.

06:28.925 --> 06:30.455
So tell me,

06:30.455 --> 06:32.953
how exactly do you need me to help?

06:33.982 --> 06:36.699
Did you finally change your mind?

06:40.467 --> 06:43.300
He's quite persuasive.

06:51.447 --> 06:52.756
[24 Hours Before the Sell-off]

06:52.756 --> 06:55.851
They sign the major affiliate sale tomorrow.

06:55.851 --> 06:57.426
You want to hold a board meeting before that

06:57.426 --> 06:59.163
and dismiss the CEO first?

06:59.163 --> 07:00.206
Exactly.

07:00.206 --> 07:01.259
Among the current board members,

07:01.259 --> 07:03.918
Director Woo opposes the sale the most.

07:03.918 --> 07:05.426
You need to meet with Director Woo

07:05.426 --> 07:07.317
and convince him to convene the board.

07:07.317 --> 07:10.056
I'm not saying I'll return to the front lines.

07:10.056 --> 07:11.759
I plan to end the long hereditary management

07:11.759 --> 07:14.763
and introduce a professional executive system.

07:14.763 --> 07:18.676
Can that happen just with your will alone?

07:18.676 --> 07:20.352
I have dedicated employees standing with me.

07:20.352 --> 07:22.686
Real change will start from the bottom up.

07:23.771 --> 07:26.441
I'm not the one leading from the front.

07:26.441 --> 07:28.318
I'm simply the person pushing from behind.

07:28.318 --> 07:30.384
Once Director Woo notifies the board,

07:30.384 --> 07:32.405
we must ensure a majority attends.

07:32.405 --> 07:33.758
We have to persuade the other directors.

07:33.758 --> 07:35.825
This is our only chance to stop the sale.

07:35.825 --> 07:38.157
We definitely don't have enough time alone.

07:38.157 --> 07:40.229
I'll ask Team 3 for some backup.

07:42.877 --> 07:44.883
Oh, there he is! Director Yoon!

07:44.883 --> 07:46.735
Yeah, that's definitely him.

08:03.061 --> 08:04.800
What is your problem with me?

08:04.800 --> 08:06.505
Please don't go.

08:14.925 --> 08:16.765
Please help us out.

08:18.743 --> 08:19.764
[Vice Chairman Jeon Seong Yeol]

08:19.764 --> 08:21.687
An emergency board meeting?

08:24.718 --> 08:28.659
So my brother finally made his move.

08:28.659 --> 08:31.424
We just need to block a majority quorum.

08:31.424 --> 08:35.730
Directors Park and Jung won't budge anyway.

08:35.730 --> 08:37.205
Get Director Ha on the line for me.

08:37.205 --> 08:38.344
Right away.

08:39.009 --> 08:40.371
Oh, and one more thing.

08:40.371 --> 08:42.467
Make sure the Trans sale contract

08:42.467 --> 08:44.144
is prepared without any hitches.

08:44.144 --> 08:46.253
Understood completely.

08:49.023 --> 08:51.819
[Three Hours Before the Sell-off]

08:56.134 --> 08:57.604
What's the status?

08:57.604 --> 08:59.367
Director Ha never showed up to the meeting.

08:59.367 --> 09:01.494
He's not answering his phone either.

09:01.494 --> 09:05.036
I think Jeon Seong Yeol swayed him.

09:09.883 --> 09:12.029
The sale contract signing is imminent.

09:19.175 --> 09:20.829
Chairman.

09:21.689 --> 09:24.759
Chairman Jeon Mu Tae is still a board member.

09:24.759 --> 09:26.676
Forget it.

09:26.676 --> 09:29.046
I have absolutely no reason to do that.

09:30.259 --> 09:32.567
This game is already over.

09:32.567 --> 09:33.985
At the general shareholders' meeting,

09:33.985 --> 09:36.988
you completely lost to that guy.

09:36.988 --> 09:39.348
I refuse to take the side of a total loser.

09:40.426 --> 09:42.175
Father.

09:42.175 --> 09:44.603
What exactly have I been fighting for?

09:45.347 --> 09:49.303
I spent my life trying to win your battles

09:49.303 --> 09:51.988
and desperately seeking your approval.

09:52.920 --> 09:56.591
Because I actually believed in the cause.

09:56.591 --> 10:00.087
The strong survive and lead Haemu.

10:00.087 --> 10:02.905
I firmly believed in that philosophy too.

10:02.905 --> 10:05.266
But take a look at Haemu's current state.

10:05.266 --> 10:08.127
Is this really the Haemu

10:09.759 --> 10:11.922
you were trying to protect?

10:13.925 --> 10:16.078
You told me yourself before.

10:16.078 --> 10:17.737
Protecting something means

10:17.737 --> 10:20.973
abandoning absolutely everything else.

10:24.060 --> 10:26.594
I came here simply to protect Haemu.

10:26.594 --> 10:30.326
I threw away my normal life, my petty pride,

10:32.739 --> 10:36.725
and even all my resentment toward you.

10:38.551 --> 10:41.212
So please, just set aside your disappointment

10:42.259 --> 10:44.509
in me for a brief moment.

10:46.349 --> 10:48.111
Do it for the sake of Haemu.

10:49.268 --> 10:52.009
[Jeon Seong Yeol]

11:15.420 --> 11:17.380
What's all this about?

11:17.380 --> 11:20.409
The sale contract you just signed is void.

11:20.409 --> 11:23.676
Vice Chairman Jeon Seong Yeol is dismissed

11:23.676 --> 11:26.175
and lacks the authority to sign contracts.

11:26.175 --> 11:28.955
What kind of total bullshit is this?

11:28.955 --> 11:32.228
We already signed and swapped the documents.

11:32.228 --> 11:35.147
On March 11, 2026, at 2:25 PM,

11:35.147 --> 11:37.942
the board officially passed your dismissal.

11:37.942 --> 11:40.487
According to Article 17 of Haemu's bylaws,

11:40.487 --> 11:42.681
all representative rights are suspended

11:43.592 --> 11:46.025
the moment the dismissal is resolved.

11:49.837 --> 11:52.081
That simply cannot be true.

11:52.081 --> 11:53.249
[Dismissal Result for VC Jeon Seong Yeol]

11:53.249 --> 11:54.967
What the hell is this?

11:54.967 --> 11:56.877
Why is this happening...

11:56.877 --> 11:58.004
Secretary Park, where is Director Ha?

11:58.004 --> 12:01.007
He is currently on standby at home.

12:01.007 --> 12:02.762
Then what's going on?

12:05.511 --> 12:06.721
Father?

12:06.721 --> 12:09.390
[Chairman Jeon Mu Tae]

12:09.390 --> 12:11.475
Why would he do this...

12:11.475 --> 12:13.500
What exactly does all this mean?

12:13.500 --> 12:16.772
We notified your company upon the dismissal.

12:16.772 --> 12:18.636
You wouldn't want the legal risks of a deal

12:18.636 --> 12:21.277
with an unauthorized representative, right?

12:21.277 --> 12:25.739
We followed all legal and bylaw procedures.

12:25.739 --> 12:28.183
If you still want to dispute its validity,

12:28.784 --> 12:30.769
we can gladly settle this in court.

12:32.413 --> 12:35.357
[Jeon Mu Tae]

12:47.570 --> 12:49.580
Since when have you been planning this?

12:50.348 --> 12:53.393
Pretending you had no interest or greed,

12:53.393 --> 12:55.670
hiding in the shadows, sharpening your claws?

12:57.376 --> 12:59.506
I didn't come here to steal what's yours.

13:00.697 --> 13:03.427
I just refused to add regrets to my life.

13:35.289 --> 13:37.342
He left in true Seong Yeol fashion.

13:37.342 --> 13:39.667
It seems they destroyed various files

13:39.667 --> 13:41.798
that could cause potential problems,

13:45.092 --> 13:47.387
but I actually have the backup right here.

13:50.227 --> 13:52.016
You're thorough as always.

13:52.826 --> 13:55.055
Though I certainly fell victim to that too.

13:57.873 --> 13:59.900
Why did you change your mind?

14:01.134 --> 14:02.736
Turns out,

14:04.662 --> 14:07.741
I wasn't quite at rock bottom after all.

14:40.958 --> 14:42.874
Man, this feels exactly like shooting a movie.

14:42.874 --> 14:45.194
Hey, it was way more dramatic than a movie.

14:45.194 --> 14:47.424
Do you know how much Hae Young and I walked?

14:47.424 --> 14:49.650
At least you guys all had partners.

14:49.650 --> 14:50.759
I was entirely on my own.

14:50.759 --> 14:53.053
I showed up at Director Min's house uninvited.

14:53.053 --> 14:54.388
You know Director Min is famous

14:54.388 --> 14:56.424
for being the most stubborn guy
on the entire board.

14:56.424 --> 14:58.794
Come on, Director Min isn't the worst.

14:58.794 --> 15:01.437
Director Yoon is the real piece of work.

15:01.437 --> 15:02.774
- Right?
- Exactly.

15:02.774 --> 15:04.545
And we managed to break him. Here.

15:05.373 --> 15:08.218
We literally almost had to board a flight.

15:14.558 --> 15:16.580
Great job out there.

15:17.704 --> 15:20.082
It's all thanks to your help.

15:20.082 --> 15:23.525
Today wouldn't have happened without you.

15:24.336 --> 15:26.105
You did well.

15:28.551 --> 15:30.991
Is Jeon Jae Yeol skipping the after-party?

15:31.884 --> 15:33.887
Why not give him a call yourself?

15:33.887 --> 15:36.253
You two meet up just fine without me anyway.

15:37.634 --> 15:39.402
It's a bit of a shame, really.

15:39.402 --> 15:41.925
If it weren't for this whole ex-boyfriend

15:41.925 --> 15:44.463
and current boyfriend dynamic, he'd be great.

15:45.979 --> 15:47.900
I mean it.

15:47.900 --> 15:50.278
There's a reason he's my girlfriend's ex.

15:50.278 --> 15:52.012
He is pretty cool.

15:52.988 --> 15:55.474
Oh, playing it cool? Not jealous at all?

15:56.217 --> 15:57.912
Why on earth would I be jealous?

15:59.229 --> 16:02.158
I'm your current boyfriend right now.

16:03.092 --> 16:05.626
Who cares? The whole team already knows.

16:05.626 --> 16:06.759
Ki Jun!

16:06.759 --> 16:07.795
What's this?

16:07.795 --> 16:09.401
Are you two holding hands right now?

16:09.401 --> 16:11.632
Holding hands openly now?

16:11.632 --> 16:14.910
You better treat us all tonight!

16:17.205 --> 16:18.523
Yes, we are holding hands!

16:18.523 --> 16:20.272
Dinner is on me tonight!

16:20.272 --> 16:22.430
She says she's treating!

16:23.602 --> 16:24.842
- How about beef?
- Really?

16:24.842 --> 16:26.463
Sounds perfect to me.

16:28.175 --> 16:30.026
Beef is way too expensive.

16:30.026 --> 16:32.387
- No beef?
- Let's just go.

16:42.579 --> 16:46.458
[One Year Later]

16:46.458 --> 16:48.737
[Head of Sales Im Hyuk Jun]

17:00.426 --> 17:02.676
The target has started moving.

17:02.676 --> 17:03.909
Over.

17:16.087 --> 17:18.682
Target is mobile. Standby team, respond.

17:48.967 --> 17:51.965
Target confirmed. We are tailing him now.

18:03.134 --> 18:04.811
Let's move.

18:44.676 --> 18:47.682
Our prediction was dead on.

18:48.300 --> 18:49.452
Let's go in.

18:51.626 --> 18:53.218
Stay sharp.

18:58.426 --> 19:00.200
We're heading in.

19:00.883 --> 19:02.116
Let's go.

19:05.432 --> 19:07.468
Are we really going in?

19:11.592 --> 19:12.929
Move over.

19:14.552 --> 19:15.969
General Manager Im!

19:19.718 --> 19:20.904
Stop right there.

19:20.904 --> 19:23.116
We're from the Audit Team.

19:23.824 --> 19:26.413
How did Audit find this place...

19:26.413 --> 19:28.120
You're supposed to be out doing sales work.

19:28.120 --> 19:30.397
What exactly are you selling here?

19:31.531 --> 19:34.428
I just needed to scrub up and polish myself

19:34.428 --> 19:37.217
to look presentable before doing sales...

19:37.217 --> 19:41.159
Slacking off at a sauna during work hours...

19:41.159 --> 19:43.343
is a blatant attendance violation, Mr. Im.

19:43.343 --> 19:46.371
Especially if you do it every single day.

19:54.380 --> 19:56.465
Rookie, are you going to snap out of it?

19:56.465 --> 19:58.339
You saw the sign to breach, didn't you?

19:58.339 --> 19:59.568
Why did you hesitate?

19:59.568 --> 20:02.488
What if we completely missed our timing?

20:02.488 --> 20:04.395
Wouldn't it have been fine anyway?

20:05.076 --> 20:06.219
What?

20:06.219 --> 20:07.786
Honestly, isn't that the truth?

20:07.786 --> 20:10.495
Audit doesn't really need to go that far.

20:10.495 --> 20:11.538
Look at me.

20:11.538 --> 20:14.666
I studied in the US with top entrance scores.

20:14.666 --> 20:16.458
So why exactly is

20:16.458 --> 20:19.550
someone like me stuck doing
this kind of grunt work...

20:24.496 --> 20:26.120
Grunt work?

20:27.652 --> 20:29.014
Who do you think you are, rookie?

20:29.014 --> 20:30.825
Do you have superpowers? Can you fly?

20:30.825 --> 20:33.394
Can you teleport? Shoot energy blasts?

20:36.883 --> 20:40.042
You're just a rookie, don't pick your tasks.

20:40.860 --> 20:43.199
Calling this grunt work...

20:43.199 --> 20:47.117
Every Audit task is equally crucial.

20:47.117 --> 20:48.308
Got it?

20:49.925 --> 20:51.834
I feel like I've heard this speech before.

20:51.834 --> 20:52.614
- Right?
- I know, right?

20:52.614 --> 20:53.580
Exactly.

20:53.580 --> 20:56.208
Alright, we caught him anyway.

20:56.208 --> 20:58.211
Great job, everyone.

20:58.211 --> 21:02.256
Must manage your health
to last long here, okay?

21:02.256 --> 21:04.699
Here, for you.

21:07.134 --> 21:09.053
And for our rookie too.

21:09.053 --> 21:10.464
Thank you so much.

21:12.934 --> 21:14.331
You smiling?

21:18.551 --> 21:19.917
Is this funny to you?

21:23.676 --> 21:24.861
I like it.

21:24.861 --> 21:27.370
Keep smiling. Smiling brings you good luck.

21:28.592 --> 21:30.152
Thank you.

21:31.660 --> 21:33.455
Here, Team 2 as well.

21:33.455 --> 21:36.259
Take good care of your health.

21:36.259 --> 21:37.925
Am I the only one weirded out?

21:37.925 --> 21:40.168
There is absolutely no middle ground, right?

21:40.168 --> 21:43.006
It feels like they're swapping personalities.

21:43.006 --> 21:45.923
They say couples resemble each other, right?

21:59.050 --> 22:00.689
How is living in a different country?

22:00.689 --> 22:02.274
How's your mom doing?

22:02.274 --> 22:04.109
I like it because it's peaceful.

22:04.109 --> 22:06.613
My mother adapted quickly as well.

22:06.613 --> 22:09.472
I just came back briefly for some work,

22:09.472 --> 22:12.102
but I never expected to see you here.

22:13.285 --> 22:14.909
You kept ignoring my calls,

22:14.909 --> 22:16.712
so I had to play a little dirty.

22:23.800 --> 22:26.173
It's a new drug project specifically targeting

22:26.173 --> 22:28.301
treatment-resistant psychiatric disorders.

22:28.301 --> 22:29.938
[CNS Innovative Drug Lab Proposal]
The roadmap is designed to expand

22:29.938 --> 22:31.429
into a medical cluster.

22:31.429 --> 22:33.175
We already signed

22:33.175 --> 22:36.559
the R&D partnership MOUs
with major domestic university hospitals.

22:36.559 --> 22:39.535
The only thing left is securing investments,

22:39.535 --> 22:43.232
but this massive project exceeds our funding.

22:44.025 --> 22:47.194
We desperately need your network and insight.

22:47.194 --> 22:48.878
[J Care Foundation CNS Research Institute]

22:53.551 --> 22:56.203
J Care Foundation went through

22:56.203 --> 22:59.499
a rough patch entirely because of me earlier.

22:59.499 --> 23:03.404
Would my stepping up really help its image?

23:03.404 --> 23:05.718
Everyone knows just how much you sacrificed

23:05.718 --> 23:08.717
to cure your mother's illness.

23:08.717 --> 23:12.327
Is there a stronger motive than your sincerity?

23:24.259 --> 23:26.232
That looks delicious.

23:29.883 --> 23:31.863
Seriously though, Mr. Noh Ki Jun,

23:31.863 --> 23:35.076
why give the rookie such a hard time at work?

23:35.076 --> 23:37.236
The poor kid looked like he was about to cry.

23:38.417 --> 23:40.585
Since when were you such a generous boss?

23:40.585 --> 23:43.009
Makes your past victims feel totally wronged.

23:43.009 --> 23:46.170
You're turning into a real boomer.

23:52.676 --> 23:55.220
This is absolutely amazing.

23:55.220 --> 23:56.804
This seems pretty easy to make, right?

23:56.804 --> 23:58.667
I should definitely try making this at home.

24:01.311 --> 24:03.029
But seriously,

24:03.029 --> 24:05.922
you seem strangely happier today.

24:13.759 --> 24:15.442
I have something to tell you.

24:15.442 --> 24:17.016
Hold on a second.

24:19.967 --> 24:21.718
I...

24:21.718 --> 24:23.545
bought a house.

24:23.545 --> 24:24.800
- A house?
- Yeah.

24:24.800 --> 24:26.001
Monthly rent? No.

24:26.001 --> 24:27.125
Jeonse? Not at all.

24:27.125 --> 24:29.005
I fully own it.

24:29.005 --> 24:31.965
It's a bit old but perfectly laid out for one.

24:31.965 --> 24:33.508
And it's really close to your place too.

24:33.508 --> 24:35.225
Isn't that awesome?

24:35.225 --> 24:38.218
Wait, were you even planning to move out?

24:38.218 --> 24:41.933
Actually, my landlord suddenly kicked me out

24:41.933 --> 24:43.818
so I was rushing to find a new place,

24:43.818 --> 24:45.729
and just happened to stumble upon a great deal.

24:45.729 --> 24:48.858
So I took the chance to buy my own place.

24:59.618 --> 25:02.029
I didn't want to stress you out

25:02.029 --> 25:03.989
over a minor housing issue like this.

25:03.989 --> 25:05.089
You're busy enough with work.

25:05.089 --> 25:07.375
We see each other every day at the office,

25:07.375 --> 25:09.211
grab dinner together after work,

25:09.211 --> 25:11.049
and even go on dates on the weekends.

25:11.049 --> 25:12.881
We share every single detail of our lives,

25:12.881 --> 25:15.592
but you had no time to discuss this with me?

25:15.592 --> 25:18.536
I'm telling you, I deliberately hid it.

25:19.568 --> 25:21.942
I hate seeing you worry about my problems.

25:23.266 --> 25:25.356
Right, I know you well enough.

25:26.104 --> 25:27.979
I'll try my best to accept

25:27.979 --> 25:29.889
that you hid your issues from me.

25:29.889 --> 25:31.734
Because that's just your personality.

25:33.109 --> 25:34.253
I'm sorry.

25:34.253 --> 25:35.864
Stop being mad, okay?

25:35.864 --> 25:38.490
But you bought a house?

25:38.490 --> 25:40.463
A place perfectly laid out for one?

25:41.277 --> 25:42.564
Does this mean

25:43.165 --> 25:45.729
you have zero intention of living with me?

25:46.873 --> 25:48.354
Well...

25:50.502 --> 25:52.671
We practically live together right now anyway.

25:52.671 --> 25:54.259
You come to my place, and I go to yours.

25:54.259 --> 25:55.216
Exactly.

25:55.216 --> 25:58.756
So why not just officially move in together?

25:59.679 --> 26:02.070
Are you asking me to move in together?

26:05.217 --> 26:06.895
Don't tell me...

26:06.895 --> 26:08.178
Marriage?

26:10.355 --> 26:11.625
Are you insane?

26:11.625 --> 26:14.109
- Insane?
- Marriage is...

26:14.109 --> 26:17.053
- Marriage simply isn't for me.
- Why is it so impossible for you?

26:17.862 --> 26:19.739
I just won't do it.

26:19.739 --> 26:22.033
I don't do things like marriage.

26:22.033 --> 26:23.620
Not even with me?

26:25.787 --> 26:27.228
Well, that's...

26:28.634 --> 26:30.830
I haven't really thought about it.

26:33.300 --> 26:35.198
Then start thinking about it right now.

26:37.924 --> 26:39.806
You're being completely one-sided about this.

26:39.806 --> 26:41.619
This is a massive decision.

26:43.346 --> 26:45.631
You once called me an unexpected variable.

26:45.631 --> 26:48.487
An unpredictable deviation in your life.

26:50.391 --> 26:52.440
I don't want to be that anymore.

26:53.149 --> 26:54.816
Ten years, twenty years down the line,

26:54.816 --> 26:58.883
I want to talk and discuss things with you

26:58.883 --> 27:01.508
and plan our future until the very end.

27:01.508 --> 27:06.134
I want to be your permanent constant.

27:06.134 --> 27:08.134
But Ki Jun,

27:08.134 --> 27:09.497
you have your own life too.

27:09.497 --> 27:12.122
It could become our shared life together.

27:12.122 --> 27:14.102
A life we fully build together.

27:38.318 --> 27:39.446
[Conclusion & Anticipated Impact]

27:39.446 --> 27:42.917
Audit independence isn't a mere chart issue.

27:42.917 --> 27:45.467
We are separating Audit from management

27:45.467 --> 27:48.161
to stop internal politics from swaying us.

27:48.161 --> 27:51.539
This restructuring ensures real independence.

27:51.539 --> 27:53.579
We will face various challenges initially,

27:53.579 --> 27:55.426
but if the company and our office are willing,

27:55.426 --> 27:58.380
this is a highly feasible system

27:58.380 --> 28:00.265
that absolutely must be implemented.

28:01.051 --> 28:03.982
That concludes my roadmap presentation.

28:06.950 --> 28:08.390
Are there any questions?

28:08.390 --> 28:11.793
Since you're all busy, please head back to...

28:15.259 --> 28:16.976
Mr. Noh.

28:18.300 --> 28:20.766
If Audit gets its own separate network,

28:20.766 --> 28:24.491
what if teams block data for security reasons?

28:24.491 --> 28:27.463
Won't we end up begging for our own data?

28:28.870 --> 28:31.371
This proposal has been approved by the board.

28:31.371 --> 28:34.499
Audit's unlimited access is now formalized,

28:34.499 --> 28:37.759
and the IT executive takes the blame for bans.

28:37.759 --> 28:39.104
What about our budget?

28:39.104 --> 28:41.584
If committee approval is needed for contracts,

28:41.584 --> 28:42.882
our agility completely dies.

28:42.882 --> 28:45.011
Only the annual total needs approval.

28:45.011 --> 28:47.412
Executions are authorized solely by the Head.

28:47.412 --> 28:51.259
Isn't that overly idealistic?

28:51.259 --> 28:53.226
You're trying to break free from management,

28:53.226 --> 28:56.313
but you just added another boss to please.

28:59.259 --> 29:01.027
You don't seem

29:01.027 --> 29:03.805
to care about pleasing anyone anyway, right?

29:05.130 --> 29:07.180
Am I completely wrong?

29:19.377 --> 29:21.217
Man, that was totally brutal.

29:21.217 --> 29:22.922
I seriously almost wet myself.

29:22.922 --> 29:24.132
I know, me too.

29:24.132 --> 29:25.300
Seriously,

29:25.300 --> 29:27.805
Mr. Noh came at the Head really hard earlier.

29:27.805 --> 29:29.471
Hey, he has every right to act like that.

29:29.471 --> 29:31.424
The head was way too harsh on him.

29:31.424 --> 29:33.558
We act oblivious, but we all remember it.

29:33.558 --> 29:35.377
She literally stood in front of reporters

29:35.377 --> 29:38.425
and openly admitted she used Ki Jun, right?

29:38.425 --> 29:40.231
She just came back without an ounce of regret.

29:40.231 --> 29:42.718
Must be super uncomfortable for him.

29:42.718 --> 29:44.070
Or maybe,

29:44.070 --> 29:45.987
do they

29:45.987 --> 29:48.283
still have something going on between them?

29:48.283 --> 29:49.451
What?

29:49.451 --> 29:51.835
Used or not, it doesn't matter.

29:51.835 --> 29:54.329
They definitely had a thing in the past.

29:54.329 --> 29:57.134
- Exactly.
- And being that openly emotional at work...

29:57.134 --> 29:58.251
That's completely false!

29:58.251 --> 30:00.384
Mr. Sung, did you catch the news?

30:00.384 --> 30:02.800
Assistant Manager Oh and Assistant Manager Sun

30:02.800 --> 30:05.615
are tying the knot. Isn't that insane?

30:08.009 --> 30:10.044
Yeah, I totally knew.

30:10.044 --> 30:11.346
He must know all about it.

30:11.346 --> 30:12.384
- Right.
- Mr. Moo.

30:12.384 --> 30:13.515
Hey, Audit Team 1.

30:13.515 --> 30:15.285
The expenses...

30:15.285 --> 30:18.085
Did you give me this quarter's expense report?

30:18.937 --> 30:20.213
Out of nowhere?

30:23.718 --> 30:25.801
Wait, hold on a second.

30:28.883 --> 30:30.416
Right now, you all...

30:32.551 --> 30:35.488
You guys are acting incredibly suspicious.

30:35.488 --> 30:37.616
Doing stocks?
I'll recommend a guaranteed hit.

30:37.616 --> 30:40.140
- Just for you.
- Really?

30:40.140 --> 30:41.300
I'm actually pretty hurt.

30:41.300 --> 30:43.946
You're hiding something from us, aren't you?

31:00.493 --> 31:01.525
Are you okay?

31:01.525 --> 31:02.596
I'm so sorry.

31:02.596 --> 31:03.635
I really apologize.

31:03.635 --> 31:04.688
I'm so sorry, Min Soo.

31:04.688 --> 31:06.592
Why did he just hit him?

31:07.634 --> 31:09.696
Why did you hit him, Hyun Gyu?

31:13.118 --> 31:15.300
- You're here?
- You're here?

31:15.300 --> 31:17.144
This way. Hurry.

31:18.468 --> 31:20.398
Take a seat, quickly.

31:46.568 --> 31:50.592
Man, you two fighting at work is terrifying.

31:50.592 --> 31:53.610
Everyone is walking on eggshells around you.

31:53.610 --> 31:54.634
And besides,

31:54.634 --> 31:56.092
if you keep failing to hide your emotions,

31:56.092 --> 31:58.563
your office romance will get instantly busted.

31:58.563 --> 32:00.284
I mean, what's the point of us trying

32:00.284 --> 32:01.824
so hard to shield you two

32:01.824 --> 32:04.463
when you make it this blatantly obvious?

32:04.463 --> 32:07.493
First, please pour each other a drink.

32:21.557 --> 32:23.980
Just repeat after me.

32:23.980 --> 32:26.397
I am truly sorry.

32:26.397 --> 32:28.566
This might feel a little cringy at first,

32:28.566 --> 32:29.984
but whenever my daughters do this exact thing,

32:29.984 --> 32:31.653
they instantly make up and move on.

32:31.653 --> 32:32.947
Just give it one try.

32:32.947 --> 32:34.610
I am sorry.

32:36.592 --> 32:38.676
- I apologize.
- I apologize.

32:38.676 --> 32:40.415
I really love you.

32:43.009 --> 32:44.878
- I love you.
- I love you.

32:44.878 --> 32:46.946
And now, cheers!

32:53.283 --> 32:55.301
- Excellent job, you two.
- Yeah.

32:55.301 --> 32:56.389
That's good, that's enough.

32:56.389 --> 32:58.217
Congratulations.

32:58.217 --> 33:01.829
But you guys must have had a massive fight.

33:02.642 --> 33:04.345
What were you even fighting about?

33:16.948 --> 33:19.784
Of course you need marriage to be happy!

33:19.784 --> 33:21.714
Working yourself to the bone all day

33:21.714 --> 33:23.871
and returning to an entirely empty house?

33:23.871 --> 33:26.166
What joy is there in a life like that, right?

33:26.166 --> 33:28.265
That actually sounds like absolute bliss to me.

33:28.265 --> 33:30.461
Dealing with annoying people at work all day,

33:30.461 --> 33:33.346
then going home to find another person there?

33:33.346 --> 33:34.768
That's purely horrifying.

33:34.768 --> 33:35.885
Da Ye,

33:35.885 --> 33:37.516
are you sick of us?

33:37.516 --> 33:39.220
She's just saying

33:39.220 --> 33:43.200
that everyone's standard for happiness varies.

33:43.200 --> 33:46.602
I've dated my boyfriend for over ten years,

33:46.602 --> 33:48.436
but I still have zero thoughts of marriage.

33:48.436 --> 33:50.189
His income is entirely unstable,

33:50.189 --> 33:53.065
and he constantly takes off for inspiration.

33:53.065 --> 33:55.278
How could I possibly ask a free spirit

33:55.278 --> 33:57.909
to buy a house, have kids, and settle down?

33:57.909 --> 34:00.342
No, but if you truly love each other,

34:00.342 --> 34:03.619
you naturally want a future side by side,

34:03.619 --> 34:06.393
and that naturally leads to wanting marriage.

34:06.393 --> 34:08.168
- Right.
- Exactly.

34:08.168 --> 34:12.496
Hey, Hyun Gyu.
If you hold onto that fantasy, stay single.

34:12.496 --> 34:13.577
Let me tell you about marriage.

34:13.577 --> 34:15.008
It is pure reality.

34:15.008 --> 34:18.593
Did your dreams of a college romance
ever come true?

34:18.593 --> 34:19.614
No, it didn't, right?

34:19.614 --> 34:21.763
Did joining a firm magically make you an adult?

34:21.763 --> 34:22.805
Not at all.

34:22.805 --> 34:24.849
You just ended up dull and fully exhausted.

34:24.849 --> 34:26.121
Marriage is the exact same thing.

34:26.121 --> 34:28.700
So does that mean we skip college and work?

34:28.700 --> 34:30.563
You only talk like that,

34:30.563 --> 34:32.492
but your own marriage is going perfectly fine.

34:32.492 --> 34:35.053
You just have to build it together.

34:35.053 --> 34:37.195
It's completely different from school or work.

34:37.195 --> 34:38.967
Those were solely my own personal choices,

34:38.967 --> 34:41.322
but marriage forces you to compromise together.

34:41.322 --> 34:42.634
The inherent risk is literally doubled.

34:42.634 --> 34:43.993
Yeah, exactly.

34:43.993 --> 34:45.119
Wait, risk?

34:45.119 --> 34:47.134
Do you approach marriage like a company audit,

34:47.134 --> 34:48.741
calculating all the possible risks beforehand?

34:48.741 --> 34:49.751
Of course.

34:49.751 --> 34:52.668
It's my life, so I must weigh risks thoroughly.

34:52.668 --> 34:56.408
By what metric do you even calculate the pros?

34:56.408 --> 34:58.634
Marriage is never about crunching the numbers.

34:58.634 --> 35:00.218
It's entirely a matter of mutual trust.

35:00.218 --> 35:01.629
Trust alone simply isn't enough.

35:01.629 --> 35:03.913
You need absolute certainty.

35:04.588 --> 35:06.909
So you're saying you lack certainty in me?

35:06.909 --> 35:08.342
Ki Jun.

35:08.342 --> 35:09.918
It's not about that at all.

35:09.918 --> 35:11.868
I'm just unsure about the massive impact

35:11.868 --> 35:14.008
marriage will have on my entire life.

35:14.008 --> 35:15.467
Ms. Joo.

35:15.467 --> 35:16.943
How exactly do I build that certainty?

35:16.943 --> 35:19.763
What do I have to do to make you certain?

35:34.634 --> 35:36.083
That was a truly fantastic meal.

35:36.083 --> 35:37.374
I'm totally stuffed.

35:37.374 --> 35:38.843
Hey, pull yourself together, man.

35:38.843 --> 35:40.003
Where should we head for round two?

35:40.003 --> 35:41.968
- Karaoke for once...
- Thanks for the meal.

35:41.968 --> 35:42.927
Thanks for treating.

35:42.927 --> 35:44.882
- We'll head out first.
- Thanks for treating.

35:44.882 --> 35:46.562
Dismissed, everybody.

35:46.562 --> 35:47.623
Get home safely.

35:47.623 --> 35:50.718
- I absolutely love karao...
- Let's go.

35:50.718 --> 35:52.412
- Take care now.
- Yes.

35:59.217 --> 36:00.662
Should I hail a cab for us?

36:00.662 --> 36:01.703
Yeah, we definitely should.

36:01.703 --> 36:03.365
It's far too long of a walk.

36:05.996 --> 36:08.313
Well, at least you're sure about the cab.

36:23.523 --> 36:25.506
Joo In Ah speaking.

36:29.967 --> 36:31.693
That's right.

37:17.181 --> 37:19.232
Thank you all for coming here.

37:20.676 --> 37:22.883
Thank you.

37:22.883 --> 37:24.222
Please take your time eating.

37:24.222 --> 37:25.935
Hold on a second.

37:30.084 --> 37:31.101
Sure.

37:31.101 --> 37:33.704
Is it really just a one-day funeral?

37:33.704 --> 37:35.648
And no condolence money at all?

37:38.334 --> 37:39.377
Yeah.

37:39.377 --> 37:41.381
She wants to keep things very quiet.

37:41.381 --> 37:43.893
But the hall feels way too empty.

37:43.893 --> 37:45.967
She forbade us from telling the staff,

37:45.967 --> 37:48.153
so only we showed up today,

37:48.153 --> 37:50.175
but it still feels wrong.

37:50.175 --> 37:52.676
They were apparently estranged for years,

37:52.676 --> 37:55.133
but she seems oddly composed.

37:55.133 --> 37:57.711
She's probably just deeply overwhelmed.

37:59.105 --> 38:00.839
Oh, Vice Chairman.

38:02.925 --> 38:04.360
You actually made it.

38:31.505 --> 38:33.735
Did you fly back just for this?

38:34.515 --> 38:36.186
There was absolutely no need for that.

38:36.186 --> 38:38.335
I actually live in Seoul these days.

38:39.138 --> 38:42.358
I'm resuming work at the foundation.

38:42.358 --> 38:44.565
That's excellent news.

38:44.565 --> 38:46.181
You made a very wise decision.

38:48.512 --> 38:52.290
Mr. Noh is standing strong here.

38:55.384 --> 38:57.171
I truly mean it.

38:57.171 --> 38:59.940
Having a guy like Ki Jun by your side

39:01.467 --> 39:03.193
is a massive relief to me.

39:10.220 --> 39:11.943
I should get going.

39:42.625 --> 39:43.911
Are you holding up alright?

39:45.883 --> 39:48.939
The hospital staff packed this for you.

39:48.939 --> 39:50.489
Your father's belongings.

39:52.384 --> 39:54.175
You must be entirely exhausted.

39:54.175 --> 39:56.305
Head home. You have work tomorrow anyway.

39:56.305 --> 39:57.767
I can handle the burial completely alone.

39:57.767 --> 39:58.936
I'm staying right here.

39:58.936 --> 40:00.350
Besides, I already took a day off.

40:00.350 --> 40:01.477
Come on, just go home.

40:01.477 --> 40:02.603
I'm perfectly fine.

40:02.603 --> 40:05.089
I'm telling you, I'm fine.

40:07.983 --> 40:09.110
Your tea is completely cold now.

40:09.110 --> 40:10.648
Let me get you a fresh cup.

41:11.426 --> 41:13.699
What's all this, seriously?

41:16.426 --> 41:18.787
What's all this?

41:23.175 --> 41:24.890
I absolutely despised him,

41:27.342 --> 41:28.961
yet I feel so incredibly sorry.

41:30.780 --> 41:33.625
I pity him but can't forgive him,

41:34.967 --> 41:38.348
but he just died before I ever could.

41:40.537 --> 41:43.134
This makes absolutely zero sense.

41:43.134 --> 41:46.078
This is so ridiculous.

41:50.547 --> 41:52.442
What's all this...

42:22.026 --> 42:24.912
I told you I can just sleep at home.

42:24.912 --> 42:27.081
You literally starved for a whole day.

42:27.081 --> 42:30.211
I need to see you eat to actually relax.

42:30.211 --> 42:32.279
What exactly are you making me?

42:38.637 --> 42:40.160
Hey.

42:42.137 --> 42:43.771
Why did you change your passcode?

42:43.771 --> 42:46.509
- I failed five times and waited five minutes.
- Hello.

42:46.509 --> 42:48.185
- Hello.
- Hello.

42:48.185 --> 42:49.759
Oh, you two were together.

42:49.759 --> 42:51.351
That's a huge relief.

42:51.351 --> 42:53.257
How have you been doing?

42:54.092 --> 42:56.068
You really should have called me first.

42:56.068 --> 42:59.119
Why mash the keypad and complain to me?

42:59.119 --> 43:01.384
- Why change the code?
- Are you asking for a beating?

43:01.384 --> 43:03.259
- You should inform me first.
- It's my house, so back off.

43:03.259 --> 43:04.800
Alright, I should leave now.

43:04.800 --> 43:05.979
- No, please stay.
- No.

43:05.979 --> 43:06.999
Join us for a meal.

43:06.999 --> 43:08.842
- I cooked some really great food.
- Right.

43:08.842 --> 43:10.482
Please sit with us.

43:12.045 --> 43:13.893
What exactly is all this food?

43:19.925 --> 43:21.886
I heard the tragic news.

43:21.886 --> 43:24.555
You must've been terribly shocked.

43:24.555 --> 43:27.933
I tried attending, but the funeral ended fast.

43:27.933 --> 43:31.092
Ki Jun fiercely insisted that I stay away.

43:31.092 --> 43:34.554
I made porridge since you likely couldn't eat.
It's incredibly easy to digest.

43:34.554 --> 43:35.941
Have some radish water kimchi too.

43:35.941 --> 43:37.610
Please eat this before it gets cold.

43:37.610 --> 43:40.446
I finely minced the innards for this...

43:40.446 --> 43:43.092
- so eat up.
- Just leave it, we can feed ourselves fine.

43:43.092 --> 43:45.953
Nonsense, it's best eaten piping hot.

43:45.953 --> 43:48.270
Thank you for the meal.

43:57.157 --> 43:59.027
This is delicious. This hits the spot.

44:00.924 --> 44:02.635
I should have added wild chives.

44:02.635 --> 44:03.759
I told you this would be delicious.

44:03.759 --> 44:05.598
Hey, you're going to give her indigestion.

44:05.598 --> 44:06.678
Ki Jun, go fetch some water for her.

44:06.678 --> 44:09.433
- She needs something to drink.
- Hurry up.

44:09.433 --> 44:11.050
That must've been completely chaotic, right?

44:11.050 --> 44:12.478
Absolutely chaotic.

44:12.478 --> 44:15.217
I did a one-day funeral for an in-law once,

44:15.217 --> 44:17.358
and it's way more hectic than a three-day one.

44:17.358 --> 44:19.662
Right now is way more chaotic.

44:19.662 --> 44:22.532
Did Ki Jun even properly assist you at all?

44:22.532 --> 44:25.152
He grew up surrounded by older women,

44:25.152 --> 44:27.842
so I highly doubt he performed like a man.

44:27.842 --> 44:31.082
Hey, stop.
Please carefully watch your word choices.

44:31.082 --> 44:32.122
Okay?

44:32.122 --> 44:33.683
What's entirely wrong with my vocabulary?

44:33.683 --> 44:35.175
Which specific word bothered you?

44:35.175 --> 44:36.384
That word does sound slightly off.

44:36.384 --> 44:37.670
- Performed?
- What's entirely wrong with that?

44:37.670 --> 44:39.682
That exact word.

44:39.682 --> 44:41.924
Oh my, you're fully a grown man now.

44:41.924 --> 44:43.158
Oh, seriously?

44:44.468 --> 44:46.702
Look at this fully grown man here.

44:48.687 --> 44:51.502
Doing his part as a man.

44:51.502 --> 44:54.520
- Absolutely adorable.
- Cut it out already, please.

44:54.520 --> 44:56.215
- Here, you eat some too.
- Hey.

45:06.092 --> 45:07.641
Taxi receipt.

45:09.092 --> 45:11.286
We can't process anything before ten.

45:11.286 --> 45:13.607
The time difference is practically nothing.

45:13.607 --> 45:14.791
Just let this one slide.

45:33.144 --> 45:35.602
I'm returning your documents.

45:35.602 --> 45:38.042
Why exactly is this being rejected?

45:38.042 --> 45:39.984
The seal certificate has the former CEO's name.

45:39.984 --> 45:42.523
You must bring one with the new CEO's name.

45:42.523 --> 45:45.524
So do I need to prepare additional documents?

45:45.524 --> 45:47.347
The full list is written right over there.

46:05.844 --> 46:08.267
To issue a completely new seal certificate,

46:08.267 --> 46:11.342
you must visit the registry office instead.

46:11.342 --> 46:15.309
Apply for continued use of the seal card first.

46:15.309 --> 46:17.147
You brought the official corporate seal, right?

46:17.147 --> 46:20.134
You need that to process the application fast.

46:20.134 --> 46:21.943
Thanks for the help.

46:21.943 --> 46:23.180
Take care.

46:36.718 --> 46:38.242
Ah Jeong.

46:50.967 --> 46:52.871
Where are you currently working?

46:53.509 --> 46:56.875
Why exactly are you asking me that?

47:04.775 --> 47:05.995
[J Care Foundation, Jeon Jae Yeol]

47:05.995 --> 47:07.969
Call me if you're interested in a job.

47:11.134 --> 47:13.295
I'm officially scouting you right now.

47:15.928 --> 47:17.350
Do I,

47:18.676 --> 47:21.303
do I even deserve an opportunity like that?

47:24.448 --> 47:27.129
I strictly need highly competent employees.

47:27.129 --> 47:28.537
That's my only criterion.

47:34.140 --> 47:37.375
So I really want to emphasize this fact.

47:37.375 --> 47:39.104
When you first joined this exact company,

47:39.104 --> 47:42.624
you were remarkably lucky to have my guidance.

47:42.624 --> 47:45.498
Because of that, you learned a massive amount.

47:45.498 --> 47:48.026
And whenever you faced severe difficulties...

47:48.026 --> 47:49.779
Just skip straight to the main point.

47:49.779 --> 47:51.113
What are you trying to tell me?

47:51.113 --> 47:54.057
Audit is finally becoming fully independent.

47:54.057 --> 47:58.495
To give the department more absolute authority,

47:58.495 --> 48:00.873
management decided to elevate the Head's rank.

48:00.873 --> 48:03.962
And you're more than qualified for this.

48:06.545 --> 48:09.975
You're getting promoted to executive.

48:16.516 --> 48:18.718
Thank you so much.

48:18.718 --> 48:20.409
- You're the best.
- Thank you.

48:23.896 --> 48:27.048
Executive Joo, please give us a short speech.

48:28.233 --> 48:31.406
This was entirely thanks to all of you.

48:31.406 --> 48:33.030
I'm truly grateful for your hard work.

48:33.030 --> 48:36.240
Oh, stop being so incredibly humble with us.

48:37.259 --> 48:39.789
Please give us your honest thoughts.
That's not fun.

48:39.789 --> 48:41.385
Too boring.

48:43.540 --> 48:44.717
Fun?

48:50.464 --> 48:53.053
Are you seriously trying

48:53.053 --> 48:55.443
to find absolute fun here in the office?

48:59.551 --> 49:01.634
In that exact case,

49:01.634 --> 49:03.627
how about this?

49:04.426 --> 49:06.129
Like this.

49:08.151 --> 49:09.984
What do you think?

49:14.634 --> 49:16.431
How do you like it?

49:18.718 --> 49:20.518
Is this entertaining enough?

49:27.542 --> 49:30.259
You don't need to do that.

49:30.259 --> 49:32.256
Since I'm getting my own private office,

49:32.256 --> 49:34.366
I won't be able to look after it often.

49:35.509 --> 49:37.260
Oh, a solo office.

49:37.260 --> 49:38.283
That sounds absolutely amazing.

49:38.283 --> 49:40.662
So, what are your plans for this evening?

49:40.662 --> 49:42.236
I'm officially treating you.

49:43.259 --> 49:44.393
Why don't you come over to my place instead?

49:44.393 --> 49:46.592
I can recreate that pasta we had last time,

49:46.592 --> 49:48.365
so I bought a huge pile of ingredients.

49:49.025 --> 49:51.482
Our executive is personally cooking for me?

49:54.175 --> 49:55.506
But unfortunately, I have some bad news.

49:55.506 --> 49:56.863
I have to head back home today.

49:56.863 --> 49:59.241
My family is making kimchi and demanded help.

49:59.241 --> 50:00.725
Oh, is that so?

50:00.725 --> 50:02.726
I guess it can't be helped then.
Go flex your muscles and help them out.

50:02.726 --> 50:04.385
Understood?

50:04.385 --> 50:05.747
- What?
- Where are you going?

50:05.747 --> 50:06.979
To my office?

50:08.342 --> 50:09.485
We're still at work.

50:09.485 --> 50:12.217
Nobody's looking.

50:12.217 --> 50:15.176
- You aren't upset, right?
- I'm furious.

50:15.176 --> 50:16.508
Ki Jun!

50:16.508 --> 50:18.308
There are plenty more cabbages outside!

50:18.308 --> 50:20.053
Bring them in!

50:20.053 --> 50:21.105
Pick up the pace.

50:21.105 --> 50:24.243
Are we donating to charity this year or what?

50:24.243 --> 50:26.187
Why on earth are we making this much kimchi?

50:26.187 --> 50:28.061
The kids barely even touch kimchi anyway.

50:28.061 --> 50:29.980
Our family has officially grown this year.

50:29.980 --> 50:31.565
What? Grown how exactly?

50:31.565 --> 50:33.038
Who's joining the family?

50:33.038 --> 50:34.943
Mom, I repeatedly told you not yet!

50:34.943 --> 50:36.862
Wait, what are you guys talking about?

50:36.862 --> 50:38.575
Why would our family size increase?

50:38.575 --> 50:41.923
We mean your boss.

50:41.923 --> 50:43.371
In Ah.

50:43.371 --> 50:46.329
She's practically family to us now!

50:46.329 --> 50:49.739
So tell me, do you have concrete plans yet?

50:49.739 --> 50:51.739
Booking a venue on a good weekend is brutal!

50:51.739 --> 50:54.338
Why are you all jumping so far ahead?

50:54.338 --> 50:55.872
Besides...

50:55.872 --> 50:58.675
She'll be insanely busy for a long while.

50:58.675 --> 51:00.027
- Why's that?
- Why's that?

51:05.229 --> 51:07.925
She just got promoted to executive.

51:07.925 --> 51:10.551
Do you know how insanely busy
an executive gets here?

51:10.551 --> 51:12.424
That's precisely who my In Ah is.

51:12.424 --> 51:14.217
She's incredibly capable and ambitious.

51:14.217 --> 51:15.426
Why would you ever try

51:15.426 --> 51:19.053
to trap such a magnificent woman
in our tiny family?

51:19.803 --> 51:23.300
Gosh, look at this brave freedom fighter.

51:23.300 --> 51:25.080
That's genuinely impressive though.

51:25.080 --> 51:28.038
Wait, isn't an Executive position
right below the Vice President?

51:28.038 --> 51:29.664
Not just anyone can reach that level.

51:29.664 --> 51:32.683
Exactly, In Ah is far from ordinary.

51:32.683 --> 51:34.902
Yeah, she'll definitely be extremely busy.

51:34.902 --> 51:37.382
Even if I can't assist someone so important,

51:37.382 --> 51:39.794
I absolutely shouldn't block her path, right?

51:39.794 --> 51:41.553
When the right time finally arrives,

51:41.553 --> 51:43.011
they'll figure it out on their own.

51:43.011 --> 51:44.554
We'll handle this entirely on our own,

51:44.554 --> 51:47.379
so please stop stressing over our timeline.

52:22.009 --> 52:23.701
This tastes absolutely incredible.

52:58.509 --> 52:59.988
In Ah!

53:01.131 --> 53:03.175
What's going on? Why the sudden call?

53:03.175 --> 53:05.577
- Is everything alright?
- Why the apron?

53:08.217 --> 53:11.224
I was making kimchi and rushed over here.

53:11.224 --> 53:14.936
You've never summoned me like this before.

53:14.936 --> 53:17.034
Ki Jun, I need to tell you something.

53:18.551 --> 53:19.854
What's it about?

53:25.718 --> 53:27.112
I...

53:28.175 --> 53:30.577
Even though things were already tough,

53:30.577 --> 53:32.988
I'm going to be significantly busier now.

53:32.988 --> 53:37.250
Early mornings, endless nights,
constant events.

53:37.250 --> 53:40.713
I might fail to reply promptly like I do now.

53:41.431 --> 53:43.354
And most importantly,

53:44.606 --> 53:46.569
I'll probably

53:47.217 --> 53:49.471
develop...

53:49.471 --> 53:51.573
a completely terrible temper.

53:52.297 --> 53:55.597
This role brings massive stress and pressure,

53:55.597 --> 53:58.104
so my patience will
definitely run much thinner,

53:58.104 --> 54:00.982
I'll get pickier, significantly angrier,

54:00.982 --> 54:03.301
and I might unfairly vent my stress on you.

54:06.700 --> 54:08.374
Okay, so...

54:10.186 --> 54:12.268
what's your main point here exactly?

54:18.676 --> 54:20.610
Do you want to move in with me?

54:22.671 --> 54:24.901
Let's finally start living together.

54:27.637 --> 54:29.306
Are you seriously asking me
to move in together?

54:29.306 --> 54:30.393
Yes, I am.

54:36.134 --> 54:38.711
Where did this sudden realization come from?

54:39.509 --> 54:41.255
Earlier today,

54:41.925 --> 54:44.505
I was entirely thrilled about the promotion,

54:44.505 --> 54:47.813
but my very first instinct was to tell you.

54:47.813 --> 54:50.988
Celebrating completely alone
felt totally empty,

54:50.988 --> 54:54.384
and that pasta tasted awful without you there.

54:54.384 --> 54:56.134
Before I even realized it,

54:56.134 --> 54:59.667
sharing every joy and sorrow became my norm.

55:01.883 --> 55:04.134
I completely failed to realize this.

55:04.134 --> 55:07.761
I was already picturing our shared daily life,

55:07.761 --> 55:11.848
but vaguely kept chanting that marriage is bad.

55:11.848 --> 55:14.432
I trapped myself in that rigid mindset.

55:16.759 --> 55:18.151
Honestly speaking,

55:19.217 --> 55:22.463
I'm still not totally confident about marriage.

55:23.342 --> 55:25.820
My own father failed to protect our family,

55:25.820 --> 55:29.240
and my mother was never part of that system.

55:29.240 --> 55:31.634
Throughout my entire life,

55:31.634 --> 55:34.182
marriage has been a totally foreign concept,

55:34.826 --> 55:36.979
so my lack of certainty's completely real.

55:38.050 --> 55:39.409
Even so,

55:40.384 --> 55:43.067
I desperately want to share my life with you,

55:43.793 --> 55:46.800
so I want to take things slowly

55:46.800 --> 55:50.799
and simply start by living together first.

56:06.551 --> 56:09.067
Hey, you need to actually give me an answer.

56:09.067 --> 56:12.012
Don't just let me ramble on completely alone.

56:15.551 --> 56:17.010
Your temper...

56:18.509 --> 56:20.813
Exactly how much worse is it going to get?

56:22.925 --> 56:24.984
Just a tiny bit?

56:29.634 --> 56:31.052
Alright then.

56:31.052 --> 56:32.437
Let's build a life together.

56:32.437 --> 56:34.243
No matter how messy it gets.

57:31.738 --> 57:35.976
That's exactly how our secret life started,

57:40.384 --> 57:43.729
filled with ordinary yet truly precious days,

57:47.634 --> 57:50.194
Gold bars, absolutely.

57:51.546 --> 57:53.618
- Merry Christmas.
- Yes.

57:54.592 --> 57:57.869
and moments that genuinely
sparkled like dreams.

58:12.066 --> 58:14.866
There were hidden sides
we never needed to know.

58:14.866 --> 58:16.470
It's so hot.

58:21.759 --> 58:24.020
Why's it absolutely freezing?

58:26.289 --> 58:28.509
No wonder I'm cold.

58:28.509 --> 58:30.193
So freezing.

58:32.883 --> 58:34.338
What the...

58:35.173 --> 58:37.199
Hey, the temperature...

58:37.199 --> 58:38.218
Oh, come on.

58:38.218 --> 58:39.387
Why do you constantly...

58:39.387 --> 58:42.163
Seriously, why is this apartment so cold?

58:43.071 --> 58:45.345
Look at this. No wonder it's freezing.

58:45.345 --> 58:48.134
And unexpected shifts in temperature.

58:48.134 --> 58:50.129
Hold on a second, okay?

58:52.300 --> 58:55.574
I repeatedly told you to keep that door open.

58:55.574 --> 58:56.592
Mold will grow everywhere!

58:56.592 --> 58:57.967
It's winter, not summer.

58:57.967 --> 59:00.824
The sewer stench ruins the living room.

59:00.824 --> 59:02.742
Will you scrub all that mold entirely alone?

59:02.742 --> 59:05.623
Fine! Since when have I ever avoided cleaning?

59:05.623 --> 59:07.772
The most critical issue was

59:11.546 --> 59:13.920
that we still had to navigate our work life

59:13.920 --> 59:15.755
completely intertwined.

59:15.755 --> 59:17.315
[Executive Joo In Ah]

59:17.315 --> 59:21.235
You only need to attend the pre-ceremony event.

59:22.592 --> 59:23.846
You seem quite upset today.

59:23.846 --> 59:25.996
Is there a major issue with this schedule?

59:25.996 --> 59:28.356
No, that's not the actual problem.

59:29.644 --> 59:32.021
I really shouldn't be acting like this.

59:32.021 --> 59:33.398
Secretary Ahn, by any chance,

59:33.398 --> 59:35.612
are you familiar with the hungry judge effect?

59:36.371 --> 59:40.113
Judges tend to hand down much harsher sentences

59:40.113 --> 59:42.282
right before their lunch break, and softer ones

59:42.282 --> 59:44.777
right after they finally eat.

59:44.777 --> 59:49.539
It proves trivial issues, like absolute hunger,

59:49.539 --> 59:52.358
can heavily impact your professional decisions.

59:53.259 --> 59:55.256
Are you extremely hungry right now?

59:55.256 --> 59:56.800
No, that's entirely missing my point.

59:56.800 --> 59:58.323
I'm just emphasizing how remarkably difficult

59:58.323 --> 01:00:00.051
separating personal life from work actually is.

01:00:00.051 --> 01:00:02.053
If you're hungry, I can prepare some snacks...

01:00:02.053 --> 01:00:04.122
Never mind, forget it.

01:00:04.122 --> 01:00:05.383
Just continue with the schedule briefing.

01:00:05.383 --> 01:00:06.472
Yes.

01:00:06.472 --> 01:00:08.141
- Exactly.
- If the event runs completely long...

01:00:08.141 --> 01:00:11.519
Separating work
and personal feelings in reality

01:00:11.519 --> 01:00:13.522
is substantially harder than it sounds.

01:00:13.522 --> 01:00:14.963
Da Young, I need an iced Americano.

01:00:14.963 --> 01:00:17.562
Add an extra shot and pack it full of ice.

01:00:17.562 --> 01:00:19.197
Understood completely.

01:00:19.197 --> 01:00:20.967
Seriously...

01:00:22.759 --> 01:00:23.827
Here it is.

01:00:23.827 --> 01:00:25.353
Thank you.

01:00:26.117 --> 01:00:28.092
- Hey.
- You scared me.

01:00:28.092 --> 01:00:29.979
Did you fight with her?

01:00:32.718 --> 01:00:34.967
But listen,

01:00:34.967 --> 01:00:37.820
I still can't get used to you working here.

01:00:40.300 --> 01:00:41.716
Can you really tell we fought?

01:00:41.716 --> 01:00:43.051
Oh, it's written all over you.

01:00:43.051 --> 01:00:45.745
Lighten up. Why advertise it?

01:00:50.892 --> 01:00:52.029
Hi.

01:01:11.300 --> 01:01:13.115
Oh, come on.

01:01:22.891 --> 01:01:24.826
I went way too far back...

01:01:28.426 --> 01:01:30.802
Sorry, I overreacted...

01:01:32.134 --> 01:01:34.560
Wait, why should I apologize first?

01:01:34.560 --> 01:01:36.983
Yeah, it was my fault.

01:01:36.983 --> 01:01:38.384
No way.

01:01:42.925 --> 01:01:45.025
Should I just apologize first?

01:01:45.025 --> 01:01:46.576
Yeah, I'll do it.

01:01:46.576 --> 01:01:49.080
Every day at work,

01:01:49.080 --> 01:01:51.513
we clash over personal feelings.

01:02:04.057 --> 01:02:06.826
It affects our work,

01:02:09.595 --> 01:02:10.809
[J Care Foundation, Jeon Jae Yeol]

01:02:10.809 --> 01:02:15.167
and work ruins our mood again.

01:02:25.092 --> 01:02:28.979
Maybe separating work and life

01:02:28.979 --> 01:02:31.227
isn't about drawing a line,

01:02:31.227 --> 01:02:34.787
but constantly finding balance.

01:02:34.787 --> 01:02:35.896
[Audit Office]

01:02:40.793 --> 01:02:42.086
Manager Noh,

01:02:42.086 --> 01:02:45.422
you need to revise the first page chart.

01:02:47.387 --> 01:02:49.594
Understood.

01:02:49.594 --> 01:02:50.800
Okay, then.

01:02:50.800 --> 01:02:52.162
He swiped it!

01:02:52.162 --> 01:02:55.543
Director Hwang put a hotel on the card again,
on a work trip!

01:02:55.543 --> 01:02:57.560
Head out now. We catch him in the act.

01:02:57.560 --> 01:02:58.692
Oh, what do we do here?

01:02:58.692 --> 01:03:02.395
Everyone except Manager Noh
has an off-site schedule.

01:03:22.134 --> 01:03:23.595
You heading out?

01:03:29.009 --> 01:03:30.891
The ice has melted a touch,

01:03:30.891 --> 01:03:33.603
so the flavor's probably opened up now.

01:03:33.603 --> 01:03:34.973
Seems a shame to waste it.

01:03:38.342 --> 01:03:40.336
You go ahead and drink it.

01:03:50.800 --> 01:03:52.598
The target's moving.

01:04:03.050 --> 01:04:05.027
He's in, too.

01:05:22.079 --> 01:05:23.442
Hi, guys.

01:05:23.442 --> 01:05:25.182
We're here from Audit.

01:05:25.182 --> 01:05:26.292
Director Hwang,

01:05:26.292 --> 01:05:29.090
the approved list for the company card,

01:05:29.090 --> 01:05:31.697
I doubt date nights made the cut.

01:05:36.259 --> 01:05:38.483
Honestly, fieldwork is the fun part.

01:05:38.483 --> 01:05:40.389
We were really in sync today.

01:05:40.389 --> 01:05:42.266
Sure.

01:05:42.266 --> 01:05:44.877
Okay, work's done, so hand it over.

01:05:48.439 --> 01:05:50.322
I'm starving. Want to grab a bite?

01:05:50.322 --> 01:05:52.122
It's cold out. How about some gamjatang?

01:05:52.122 --> 01:05:53.602
The kind that's all bubbling away.

01:05:53.602 --> 01:05:56.467
We came all the way to a hotel.
Let's go to a nice restaurant.

01:05:56.467 --> 01:05:58.032
Fine?

01:05:58.032 --> 01:06:00.201
I'm fine, thank you.

01:06:00.201 --> 01:06:01.873
And you?

01:06:01.873 --> 01:06:02.902
And you?

01:06:02.902 --> 01:06:04.413
That's not funny. Come on.

01:06:04.413 --> 01:06:05.566
Come on.

01:06:05.566 --> 01:06:06.791
Looks like you're about to laugh.

01:06:06.791 --> 01:06:08.376
See? You laughed. Look, you totally did.

01:06:08.376 --> 01:06:10.044
My boss made a joke, so I laughed.

01:06:10.044 --> 01:06:13.465
Yeah, right. You laughed because it was funny.

01:06:13.465 --> 01:06:14.799
Fine, let's go get gamjatang.

01:06:14.799 --> 01:06:15.906
Sounds good.

01:06:15.906 --> 01:06:17.426
- And,
- Yeah?

01:06:17.426 --> 01:06:20.050
- I'm sorry.
- For what?

01:06:20.050 --> 01:06:21.538
This morning.

01:06:23.061 --> 01:06:26.342
Honestly, I felt bad too,
for blowing up like that.

01:06:26.342 --> 01:06:28.024
Let's not fight, okay?

01:06:28.024 --> 01:06:30.798
Yeah, let's really stop fighting.

01:06:58.300 --> 01:06:59.952
Let's roll.

01:07:03.472 --> 01:07:05.217
Follow that car up ahead, please.

01:07:05.217 --> 01:07:07.134
Hold on.

01:07:07.134 --> 01:07:09.211
The reason you got close with James...

01:07:14.300 --> 01:07:17.010
You can't look sloppy in front of your boss.

01:07:18.195 --> 01:07:21.158
You can't look sloppy in front of your boss.

01:07:21.158 --> 01:07:22.597
I'm sorry.

01:07:23.784 --> 01:07:25.081
Cut.

01:07:27.551 --> 01:07:29.665
Well, you broke the gun.

01:07:29.665 --> 01:07:31.071
Oh, got it.

01:07:42.464 --> 01:07:44.955
Hey, why is this thing so easy to win?

01:07:45.931 --> 01:07:47.291
I...

01:07:57.009 --> 01:07:59.157
- Don't overdo it.
- Got it.

01:07:59.157 --> 01:08:00.821
Don't worry about Mr. Ahn.

01:08:00.821 --> 01:08:02.848
I'm sorry, let me take it again.

01:08:05.587 --> 01:08:07.082
Salt?

01:08:07.082 --> 01:08:08.684
We've got to redo this one.

01:08:11.253 --> 01:08:13.709
You can't just leave him like that.
Do something!

01:08:13.709 --> 01:08:15.215
I'm sorry.

01:08:21.073 --> 01:08:23.213
Sale Contract Signing.

01:08:23.213 --> 01:08:26.676
Tomorrow there's a sale contract
for a key affiliate...

01:08:26.676 --> 01:08:28.415
A sale contract signing...

01:08:32.759 --> 01:08:35.217
It was like,
"How about a kiss since we're here?"

01:08:35.217 --> 01:08:37.608
Don't say something like, "Want to go there?"

01:08:37.608 --> 01:08:39.050
Why did you...

01:08:39.050 --> 01:08:41.988
- What?
- Why are you laughing?

01:08:46.121 --> 01:08:49.520
- Why is this so hot?
- It's burning, why's it so hot?
